SUMMARY:Found Footage Fest: Porcelain VHS Treasures
DTSTART:20260911T020000Z
DTEND:20260911T034500Z
DTSTAMP:20260911T020000Z
UID:0wrIiPLbH1
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 90 mins (1h30m)\n\nLive comedy with VHS tapes!BRAND 
 NEW VOLUME 11 SHOW FOR 2026! Joe Pickett (The Onion) and Nick Prueher (La
 te Show With David Letterman) have over 14\,000 VHS tapes in their clutter
 ed office in Brooklyn and will take viewers on a guided tour of their late
 st/greatest finds in this brand new Volume 11 show for 2026. Highlights in
 clude a psychotic dollar store salesman\, a video catalog of frightening p
 orcelain dolls\, two wonderfully homemade Bigfoot videos and a new age “
 miracle” treatment from the 80s called “Psychic Surgery.” (Contains 
 nudity\, language\, clowns)“I think I speak for fans everywhere when I e
 xpress gratitude for their continued hunt for hilariously bad videos. I ho
 pe the search never ends.”— Steven Hyden\, Uproxx\n\nhttps://www.siff.
 net/cinema/in-theaters/found-footage-festival-porcelain-vhs-treasures\n\nE
 stimated start: 19:15
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Faust with the Invincible Czars (1926)
DTSTART:20260910T020000Z
DTEND:20260910T040500Z
DTSTAMP:20260910T020000Z
UID:RE6gW4b3PE
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 106 mins (1h46m)\n\nThe Invincible Czars celebrate 1
 00 years of the silent masterpiece Faust (1926\, FW Murnau). Their brand n
 ew electrifying score marries new and old elements of classical music\, bo
 ssa nova and even a touch of heavy metal to bring the movie to life for co
 ntemporary audiences and incorporates a mix of instruments like flute\, vi
 olin and electric guitar.  Celebrate 100 years of SIFF Cinema Uptown wit
 h this 100 year old film! *Live music by The Invincible Czars*\n\nhttps:/
 /www.siff.net/cinema/in-theaters/faust-with-the-invincible-czars\n\nEstima
 ted start: 19:15
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
